class.description:
Paths are [code]smb://host[/code] (the host's shares), [code]smb://host/share/folder/...[/code] (a folder on a share) or local paths. SMB paths are not URL-encoded: names with spaces, [code]#[/code] or [code]%[/code] are written as they are. SMB2 and SMB3 (with signing; no Kerberos, no SMB1), logged in with the credentials given by [method set_smb_credentials] for the host, else as guest.
Every call blocks for network round trips (up to [member timeout] seconds each when a host doesn't answer): call it from a worker thread, for example a [WorkerThreadPool] task. One connection is kept per object and reused while the host and share stay the same; a connection the server dropped meanwhile is replaced once, silently. Calls on one object are serialized.
[codeblock]
MediaBrowser.set_smb_credentials("192.168.2.10", "user", password, "")
var browser := MediaBrowser.new()
var entries := browser.list_dir("smb://192.168.2.10/Films")
if entries.is_empty() and browser.get_last_error() != "":
    print(browser.get_last_error())
[/codeblock]
